what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back again with another installment  of our beyond omega level series where  we cover the most powerful characters in  comics and today we're talking about  perhaps spider-man's most deadly villain  the red goblin now the first appearance  of the red goblet occurred in the  amazing spider-man number 798 by dan  slott and stewart imminent of course  this was in 2018 during dan's slot's  final story arc of his long run and  amazing run on amazing spider-man and  basically what happens is that norman  osborne which of course is the real name  of the green goblin one of spider-man's  oldest and most bitter enemies is  basically sick of losing to spider-man  all the time so he decides he's going to  find a way to fight and defeat his  archrival so he steals the carnage  symbiote from a shield warehouse now i'm  pretty sure all of you know what the  carnage symbiote is but in case you  don't i'll give you the extremely  condensed version so spider-man is taken  to a planet called battle world by a guy  called the beyonder where he's basically  bonded with an alien symbiote that he  would eventually abandon which made the  symbiote pretty pissed off later the  symbiote would bond to eddie brock who  was also pissed off at spider-man and in  their mutual hatred they became venom  and when sharing a jail cell with a  serial killer named cletus cassidy the  venom symbiote basically left behind an  offspring which bonded with cletus and  then became carnage now something else  that i want to point out here is that  spider-man had also taken away norman  osborne's ability to become the green  goblin and so in truth the hope of  norman osborn was to bond with the  carnage symbiote in order to restore his  ability to become the green goblin the  other part of that is that norman had a  really hard time controlling the  symbiont because it was basically  motivated by a desire to kill as many  people as possible but he's eventually  able to reason with the symbiote as it  allows him to have more control so that  he can put his plan to kill spider-man  in motion but after his memory is jogged  so that he remembers spider-man's secret  identity norman osborn confronts peter  parker at the daily bugle as the red  goblin and basically tells them that if  he doesn't stop operating as spider-man  he'll kill everyone that's important to  peter and when i say everyone i mean  like everyone now norman also takes a  piece of the carded symbiote and then  merges it with his grandson normie to  create the goblin child which is  essentially just a small version of the  red goblin and it's just really as  creepy looking as it sounds it really is  now norman also plants a piece of the  carnage symbiote inside of peter's loved  ones and threatens that he can command  these pieces of the symbiote to kill  their hosts at any point in time but  flash thompson is able to save mary jane  and aunt may by removing the pieces of  the carnate symbiote now the red  goblin's quest to defeat spider-man  comes to a head when the two of them  battle in times square while peter's  wearing the venom symbiote and while red  goblin gains the advantage at first  spider-man is able to mess with his head  by getting norman to doubt his own  abilities by pointing out that he needed  the carnage symbiote in order to win and  so the battle ends with spider-man using  a gas tank to destroy the carnage  symbiote and the whole ordeal causes  norman to go insane and think that he  actually is cletus cassidy while  spider-man is norman osborne now as for  his powers they come from two very  different sources obviously the carnage  symbiote is one of those sources but  it's also enhanced by the goblin serum  now the goblin serum was the substance  that first transformed osborne into the  green goblin which granted him a variety  of powers like superhuman strength speed  stamina and reflexes as well as a  moderate healing factor now even before  being injected with the serum norman  osborne was pretty intelligent but the  serum took his intelligence to the next  level and he basically became a genius  however this boost to his intelligence  comes with a drawback in that the serum  also seems to cause norman osborne to  become mentally unstable to the point of  insanity now as we mentioned at one  point norman lost the abilities granted  to him by the goblin serum after dr  octopus as superior spider-man injected  him with an anti-serum that counteracts  its effects but upon merging with a  carnot symbiote the anti-serum is purged  from his system and the green goblin is  able to work again but we also have the  carnage symbiote giving norman osborne  powers as well so most notably this is  going to make norman osborne even  stronger faster and more durable than he  is with the goblin serum and just in  terms of physical strength carnage is  said to be stronger than spider-man and  venom combined now the carnage symbiote  is also capable of shape-shifting and  its hosts frequently use this ability to  turn their appendages into weapons like  axes or swords and also mimic  spider-man's web slinging abilities now  the red goblin in particular uses this  ability to recreate his goblin glider  which he uses to fly around and an  updated version of his famous pumpkin  bombs that he very creatively names  carnage bombs and which actually seem to  have somewhat of a mind of their own  with the capability to speak and to bite  their victims he can also heal most  injuries instantaneously including the  loss of his limbs now traditionally the  carnot symbiote has had a weakness to  fire and sound but the red goblin does  not seem to share these weaknesses as  he's routinely been near fire with no  ill effects and can even breathe fire  for some reason it's never really  explained but he can however he does  retain one of carnage's traditional  weaknesses which is the touch of the  anti-venom symbiote which was worn by  flash thompson during this storyline now  it's time to address the elephant in the  room the thing you've probably been  thinking ever since you clicked on this  video is red goblin really omega level  and to that i answer an emphatic maybe  does he have the feats to be considered  omega level probably not but he does  have impressive feats he's defeated some  incredibly powerful opponents including  venom anti-venom miles morales silk and  doc ock he's even defeated the human  torch which is definitely his most  impressive feat since the human torch is  beyond omega level in his own right but  is taking him out enough to make a  character omega level or beyond probably  not but could the red goblin  theoretically do something that would  cause us to consider him omega level and  the answer to that is yes now he's not  going to destroy the planet in the  traditional sense by blowing it up he's  not that sort of a threat but that's not  to say he couldn't destroy everyone  living on the planet in fact i think he  could in much the same way that he  threatened to kill mary jane and aunt  may by sending fragments of the carnage  symbiote into their brain he could  theoretically do the same thing to  everybody in the world would that take  some extensive planning by someone with  a very keen and genius level intellect  sure but norman osborne fits that bill  he's smart enough and cruel enough to  pull something like that off and if he's  going to wipe out all of the human life  on the planet then i don't think that's  a big stretch to call him omega level  now it is a little bit of a stretch to  calm omega level in general but hey work  with me here guys work with me with that  being said we're gonna bring this to an  end  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

